From e7db7113f2ef4fbc06d3795a78d8804d5aa16483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Agnya <manthram@Pradass-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 20:20:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Fix broken and unreliable internal navigation links
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- "Report this trip" pointed to a page that never existed (/report-trip/:id);
  replaced with a working report modal wired to the existing /api/reports
  endpoint, matching the pattern already used for reporting users.
- Six chat links across chat-inbox, quick-trip-detail, and trip-requests
  pointed to /chat/:id, which doesn't match the registered /chat-buddy/:threadId
  route — fixed to the correct path.
- Replaced ~20 window.location.href assignments and a couple of raw <a href>
  tags used for in-app navigation (trip cards, profile links, FAQ, Community,
  browse/post CTAs, sign-in page legal links) with wouter's client-side
  routing, consistent with how the rest of the app navigates. Sign-in/sign-out
  redirects were left as hard reloads intentionally.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
